From 0576b0dbc5d3561c8426da700951962dbbb7ffe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:06:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/exynos: decon7: latch the window disable before
 suspending

decon_atomic_disable() states its own requirement in a comment: every
window has to be disabled before the connector is suspended, or the
block may later scan out of a destroyed buffer. It does not meet it.

decon_disable_plane() asserts the shadow protection of the window,
clears WINCONx_ENWIN, asks for a standalone update and leaves the
protection asserted. On the commit path that is correct, because
decon_atomic_flush() releases the protection of every window right
afterwards and the write is latched there. An atomic disable is not
followed by a flush, so the protection stays on, the ENWIN clear never
reaches the shadow registers, and pm_runtime_put_sync() follows without
waiting for the frame in flight.

DECON is therefore suspended still configured on the framebuffers it was
scanning, and resumes from that configuration. When the compositor drops
its last reference to one of those buffers the mapping is torn down
while the block is still fetching from it, and the SysMMU fault handler
panics:

  exynos-sysmmu 14860000.iommu: 14830000.display-controller: [READ]
  PAGE FAULT occurred at 0xf20061c0
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Unrecoverable System MMU Fault!
   exynos_sysmmu_irq+0xc4/0x150
   __iommu_unmap+0x148/0x324
   iommu_dma_free+0x2c/0x50
   exynos_drm_gem_destroy+0x9c/0xd4
   drm_gem_dmabuf_release+0x40/0xa0
   dma_buf_release+0x40/0x9c

On gtaxlwifi the panic lands 297 ms after the panel wake and is
reproduced by cycling the screen off and on.

Release the protection, ask for the update and wait for the vsync that
makes the disable effective before the clocks go, which is what
decon_clear_channels() in this same file already does for the channels
it finds enabled at probe.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
index 3f8ff3ae9b..7e8bfe4cd3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
@@ -744,6 +744,7 @@ static void decon_atomic_enable(struct exynos_drm_crtc *crtc)
 static void decon_atomic_disable(struct exynos_drm_crtc *crtc)
 {
 	struct decon_context *ctx = crtc->ctx;
+	u32 val;
 	int i;
 
 	/*
@@ -754,6 +755,22 @@ static void decon_atomic_disable(struct exynos_drm_crtc *crtc)
 	for (i = 0; i < WINDOWS_NR; i++)
 		decon_disable_plane(crtc, &ctx->planes[i]);
 
+	/*
+	 * decon_disable_plane() leaves the shadow protected: on the commit
+	 * path decon_atomic_flush() releases it, but nothing flushes after
+	 * an atomic disable, so without this the clear above never reaches
+	 * the shadow registers and the block keeps the old buffers.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < WINDOWS_NR; i++)
+		decon_shadow_protect_win(ctx, i, false);
+
+	val = readl(ctx->regs + DECON_UPDATE);
+	val |= DECON_UPDATE_STANDALONE_F;
+	writel(val, ctx->regs + DECON_UPDATE);
+
+	/* Disabling a channel only takes effect at the next vsync. */
+	decon_wait_for_vblank(ctx);
+
 	ctx->scanout_on = false;
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(ctx->dev);
 }
-- 
